            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            electrically charged under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            is the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric-magnetic+duality"} electric-magnetic duality
            is the M5-brane.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#as_a_greenschwarz_type_sigmamodel As a Green-Schwarz type sigma-model
          %p
            As a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            %a{:href => "#BLNPST97"} BLNPST 97
          %h3#as_a_black_brane
            As a black
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            solution of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            the M5-brane is given (
            %a{:href => "#Gueven92"}> Gueven 92
            ) by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 5
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 5
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{5,1} \times (\mathbb{R}^5-\{0\})
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 5
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g = H^{-1/3} g_{\mathbb{R}^{5,1}} \oplus H^{2/3} g_{\mathbb{R}^5-\{0\}}
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = 1 + \frac{1}{r}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            the distance in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^5
            from the origin, and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            being
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 5
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F = \star_{\mathbb{R}^5} \mathbf{d}H
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS state
            of 11-dimensional supergravity.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of this spacetime is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS7
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} S4
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} AdS-CFT
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                1/2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"} F1-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraneSolutionsInSupergravity.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (table from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "black+brane#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13"} Blumenhagen, Lüst &amp; Theisen 2013, Chapter 18.5
          %h3#AtAnOrbifoldSingularity At an orbifold singularity
          %p#NearHorizonOrbifold
            More generally for 1/2 BPS black M5-branes, the near horizon geometry is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi AdS
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7 \times S^4/G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"}> ADE subgroup
            ) acting by left multiplication on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
            in the canonical way, under the identitfication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 \simeq S(\mathbb{R}^5) \simeq S(\mathbb{R}\oplus \mathbb{H})
            (
            %a{:href => "#MFF12"}> MFF 12, section 8.3
            ).
          %p
            While this geometric discussion in
            %a{:href => "#MFF12"} MFF 12, section 8.3
            works for all the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroups of SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            the M5-branes appear only at A-type singularities, while the more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+field+theories"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal field theories
            for all possible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
            appear only after passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#ZHTV14"}> ZHTV 14, p. 3
            ).
          %p
            On the other hand, when placing the M5 at an MO5-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten95"}> Witten 95
            ) its worldvolume theory breaks from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
            to
            = succeed "-supersymmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0)
          %p (…)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#worldvolume_theory Worldvolume theory
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of the M5-brane is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory involves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            kind (
            %a{:href => "#Witten07"}> Witten07
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten09"} Witten09
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+a+2-bundle"} connections on a 2-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AUT(G)
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            For instance in the proposal of (
            %a{:href => "#SSW11"}> SSW11
            ) one sees in equation (2.1)
            %em almost
            the data of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞𝔲𝔱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{aut}(\mathfrak{g})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid+of+Lie+2-algebra+valued+forms"} Lie 2-algebra valued forms
          %h3#branes_inside_the_m5 Branes inside the M5
          %p
            The M5-brane admits two solitonic excitations (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-branes within branes)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 1
                \: the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+string"} self-dual string
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 3
                \: the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-brane+in+6d"} 3-brane in 6d
                (see there for more)
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5+brane+bound+state"} M2-M5 brane bound state
          %h3#dimensional_reduction Dimensional reduction
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} dimensional reduction
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            on a circle the M5-brane turns into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D4-brane
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} compactification
            of the 5-brane on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            yields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#ConstructionByCompactificationOf5Branes"} N=2 D=4 SYM – Construction by compactification of 5-branes
          %h3#holographic_dual Holographic dual
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            for the 5-brane is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi CFT
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7/CFT_6
            and relates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-dimensional+supergravity"} 7-dimensional supergravity
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} reduction
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            on a 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            to an asymptotically 7d
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
          %h3#7dCSDual Conformal blocks and 7d Chern-Simons dual
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-field" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual 2-connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            M5-brane is supposed to have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            description in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 1996
            ). We discuss the relevant “fractional”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            that defines the correct
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle with connection
            on a 7-dimensional manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with boundary the M5-brane, thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            down to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-dimensional+supergravity"} 7-dimensional supergravity
          %p
            As discussed there, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            on these 3-connections is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∪
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat G_4 \mapsto
                  \\exp(i \int_X \hat G_4 \cup \hat G_4)
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i \int_X (-))
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to the point
            %li
              %p
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson-Deligne+cup+product"} Beilinson-Deligne cup product
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} 7-connection
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mn 4
                        %mo ∪
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G_4 \cup \hat G_4
          %p
            The space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            of this 7d theory on the M5 worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial X
            would be the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-supersymmetric+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-supersymmetric QFT
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
          %p
            Except, that it turns out that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            is
            %em twice
            that required from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %p
            Therefore the above action functional is not yet the correct one, but only a fractional version of it is. However, the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∪
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4 \cup G_4
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            has in general no reason to be divisible by 2.
          %p
            This is related to the fact that as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H^4(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+refinement"} quadratic refinement
            of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\hat G, \hat G') \mapsto \exp(i \int_X \hat G \cup \hat G')
                  \\,,
          %p
            but of twice that. In (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 1996
            ) it was argued, and later clarified in (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger"}> Hopkins-Singer
            ), that instead the action functional should be replaced by a proper
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+refinement"} quadratic refinement
          %p
            This is accomplished by shifting the center of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
            by a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
            of the degree-4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_4 \in H^4(X, \mathbb{Z}/2)
            from 0 to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}\lambda
          %p
            (For that to make sense in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            happens to be divisible by 2 on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger"} Hopkins-Singer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is divisbible by 2.)
          %p
            Since
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            it follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}p_1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\frac{1}{2}p_1 \; mod \; 2)
                  \\;
                  \=
                  \\;
                  \\nu_4 \in H^4(X, \mathbb{Z}/2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the very definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \alpha \in \hat H^4(X)
            the combination
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo +
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mover
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat \alpha \cup \hat \alpha + \hat \alpha \cup \hat \lambda = Sq^4(\hat \alpha) - \hat \alpha \cup \hat \lambda
                  \\; =\;  0 \;  mod  \; 2
          %p is divisible by 2.
          %p Therefore define then the modified quadratic form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi exp
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∪
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∪
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(i S^\lambda)
                  \\; : \;
                  \\hat a \mapsto \exp i \int_X
                  \\frac{1}{2}
                  \\left(
                  \\hat a \cup \hat a
                  +
                  \\hat a \cup \hat \mathbf{\lambda}
                  \\right)
          %p
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
            for the definition of the differential refinement
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathbf{\lambda} = \frac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{p}_1
          %p
            Notice that where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat a = 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat a = - \frac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{\lambda}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\frac{1}{2}\lambda
            here a
            %em
              background
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            for the 7-d Chern-Simons theory.
          %p
            This is now indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+refinement"} quadratic refinement
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection+pairing"} intersection pairing
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mi i
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo +
                      %mover
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo )
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo )
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo )
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp i \left(
                  S^\lambda\left(\hat a + \hat b \right)
                  \-
                  S^\lambda\left( \hat a \right)
                  \-
                  S^\lambda\left( \hat b \right)
                  +
                  S^\lambda\left( 0 \right)
                  \\right)
                  \=
                  \\exp i \int_X ( \hat a \cup \hat b  )
                  \\,.
          %p
            To express the correct action functional for the 7d Chern-Simons theory it is useful to define the shifted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat a  := \hat G_4 - \frac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{\lambda}
                  \\,,
          %p
            which the object whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            with respect to the 7d Chern-Simons theory are still
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat a = 0
          %p
            Then in terms of the original
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G_4
            the action functional for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
            reads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∪
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(i S(\hat G_4))
                  \=
                  \\exp(i \int_X
                  \\frac{1}{2}
                  (
                  \\hat G_4 \cup \hat G_4
                  \-
                  (\frac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{\lambda})^2
                  )
                  )
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the action as it appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten96, (3.6)
            ).
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
            we may summarize the outcome of this reasoning as follows:
          %p
            %em>
              The divisibility of the action functional requires a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2(G_4 - a)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Wu+structure"} twisted Wu structure
              in
              = succeed "-cohomology." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2(G_4 - a)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string+structure"} twisted differential string structure
              known as the “Witten quantization condition” on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            \.
          %h3#RestrictionOfTheCField
            Restriction of the supergravity
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            We discuss the conditions on the restriction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            on the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            to the M5-brane.
          %p
            This is similar to the analogous situation in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten anomaly cancellation
            condition demands that the restriction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 3
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H_3 \hat H^3(X)
            on spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \hookrightarrow X
            has to trivialize, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel-Whitney+class"} Stiefel-Whitney class
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_3 = \beta(w_2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bockstein+homomorphism"} Bockstein homomorphism
            induced from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mn 2
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z} \stackrel{\cdot 2}{\to}
                    \\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Q
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_3|_Q \simeq W_3
                  \\,,
          %p
            thus defining a
            %span.newWikiWord
              twisted spin^c-structure
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/twisted+spin%5Ec-structure"} ?
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
          %p
            The analog of this for the M5-brane is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten2000"}> Witten00, section 5
            ). There it is argued that there is a class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta \in H^3(Q, U(1))
          %p
            on the 5-brane such that under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bockstein+homomorphism"} Bockstein homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta'
            induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R} \to U(1)
            we have for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G \in \hat H^4(X)
            the condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Q
                  %mo =
                  %mi β
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G|_Q = \beta'(\theta)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the
            %a{:href => "#7dCSDual"} above
            quantization condition, this may also be thought of as witnessing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+string+structure"} twisted string structure
            on the 5-brane (
            %a{:href => "#Sati10"}> Sati
            ).
          %p
            This condition reduces to the above one for the
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            on the circle.
          %h3#m5brane_charge M5-brane charge
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane+charge"} M5-brane charge
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#AnomalyCancellation Anomaly cancellation
          %p
            Consider a 2-parameter family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 11
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(11)}
            of 11-dimensional
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            and a 2-parameter family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 11
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{M5} \hookrightarrow X^{(11)}
            of 6-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolumes"} worldvolumes
            of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundles"} normal bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_X Q_{M5}
            of this inclusion carries a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
          #eq:IM5.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi I
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I^{M5}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  I^{M5}_{\psi}
                  +
                  I_{C}
                  \\;\in\;
                  H^8(F \times Q_{M5},\mathbb{Z})
          %p where
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the first summand is the class of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+anomaly"} chiral anomaly
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+fermions"} chiral fermions
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{M5}
                (
                %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96, (5.1)
                ),
            %li
              %p
                the second term the class of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual higher gauge field
                (
                %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96, (5.4)
                )
          %p
            Moreover, there is the restriction of the
            = succeed "-term" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/I8"} I8
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "I8#eq:TheTerm"} there
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{M5}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mn 11
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{11}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{M5}
            (the “anomaly inflow” from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+spacetime"} bulk spacetime
            to the M5-brane)
          #eq:I8AnomalyInflow.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 8
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I_8\vert_{M5}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  I_8
                  \\big(
                  T_{Q_{M5}} X
                  \\big)
                  \\;\in\;
                  H^8(F \times Q_{M5},\mathbb{Z})
                  \\,.
          %p
            The sum of these cohomology classes, evaluated on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+class"} fundamental class
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{M5}
            is proportional to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Pontryagin+class"} second Pontryagin class
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
          #eq:SumOfM5AndInflowAnomalyIsp2.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mn 8
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 24
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I^{M5}
                  \\;+\;
                  I_8\vert_{M5}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{24} p_2(N_{Q_{M5}})
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96 (5.7)
            )
          %p
            This result used to be “somewhat puzzling” (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96, p. 35
            ) since consistency of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            should require its total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
            to vanish. But
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2(N_{Q_{M5}})
            does not in general vanish, and the right conditions to require under which it does vanish were “not clear” (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96, p. 37
            ).
          %p
            (For more details on computations involved in this and the following arguments, see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BilalMetzger03"} Bilal-Metzger 03
          %p
            A resolution was proposed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FreedHarveyMinasianMoore98"} Freed-Harvey-Minasian-Moore 98
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BahBonettiMinasianNardoni18"} Bah-Bonetti-Minasian-Nardoni 18 (5)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BBMN19"} BBMN 19 (2.9) and appendix A.4, A.5
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_8
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:I8AnomalyInflow"} (2)
            but would be all of the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
          #eq:FiberIntegration.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 6
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 4
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 4
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 4
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 4
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mn 8
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 24
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msubsup
                            %mi G
                            %mn 4
                            %mrow
                              %mi M
                              %mn 5
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\pi_\ast
                  \\Big(
                  \-
                  \\tfrac{1}{6}
                  G_4  G_4  G_4
                  +
                  G_4  I_8
                  \\Big)
                  \&amp; =
                  \- \tfrac{1}{24} p_2 + \tfrac{1}{2}([G^{M5}_4])^2 + I_8
                  }
          %p
            Here we used (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Spin5#FiberIntegrationOfCupPowersOfChiOver4Sphere"} this Prop
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi χ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_\ast\big(
                  \\chi^3
                  \\big)
                  \\;=\;
                  2 p_2
                  \\,,
          %p
            which would thus cancel against the first term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 24
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{24} p_2
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FiberIntegration"} (4)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SumOfM5AndInflowAnomalyIsp2"} (3)
            would be canceled… except for yet one last remaining term (shown as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∝
                  %msubsup
                    %mi γ
                    %mn 4
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \propto \gamma_4^2
            in
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#BBMN19b"} BBMN 19b (4.9), (4.13), (5.22)
          #eq:RemainingAnomaly.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                    %mrow
