          %h2#References References
          %h3#survey Survey
          %p The history as of the 1990 is reviewed in:
          %ul
            %li#Duff99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              , chapter 3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"} ISBN:9780750306720
          %p Further reviews and general accounts include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robbert+Dijkgraaf"}> Robbert Dijkgraaf
                ,
                %em The mathematics of fivebranes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/hep-th/pdf/9810/9810157v1.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometric+and+topological+structures+related+to+M-branes"} Geometric and topological structures related to M-branes
                (2010)
          %h3#ReferencesAsBlackBrane Black brane description
          %h4#unwrapped Unwrapped
          %p
            The M5 was first found as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+fivebrane"} black fivebrane
          %ul
            %li#Gueven92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rahmi+Gueven"}> Rahmi Gueven
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Black
                    = succeed "-brane" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 11
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 11
                    supergravity theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(92)90540-K"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(92)90540-K
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/338203"} spire:338203
              %p also in:
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                (ed.),
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
                (1999) 135-141
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li#DuffLu94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jian+Xin+Lu"} Jian Xin Lu
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Black and super
                  = succeed "-branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %strong 416
              (1994) 301-334 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9306052"}> arXiv:hep-th/9306052
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(94)90586-X"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(94)90586-X
          %p
            That this metric, as well as that of every black
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            brane for
            %em odd
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Horowitz"} Gary Horowitz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher-dimensional resolution of dilatonic black hole singularities
              %strong 12
              (1995) 297-318 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9410073"}> arXiv:hep-th/9410073
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/12/2/004"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/12/2/004
          %p
            Classification of more general M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                S. Ferrara, A. Kehagias, H. Partouche, A. Zaffaroni,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Membranes and Fivebranes with Lower Supersymmetry and their AdS Supergravity Duals
                %strong 431
                (1998) 42-48 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9803109"}> arxiv:hep-th/9803109
                )
            %li#MFF12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Half-BPS M2-brane orbifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.4761"} arXiv:1007.4761
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1408561553"} Euclid
          %p also to some extent in
          %ul
            %li
              Changhyun Ahn, Kyungho Oh, Radu Tatar,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Orbifolds
