                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X25500230"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X25500230
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (concrete example of the
                  %a{:href => "AdS-CFT+correspondence#ReferencesMicroscopicAdSCFTViapBraneSigmaModesl"} holographic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+formalism"} superembedding
                  of the probe M5 into its own
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi AdS
                          %mn 7
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
          %p
            Amplification that the resulting B-field on the M5-brane is
            %em not naively
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual
          %ul
            %li#HoweSezginWest97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+S.+Howe"}> Paul S. Howe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+C.+West"} Peter C. West
              = succeed "," do
                %em The six-dimensional self-dual tensor
              %strong 400
              3–4 (1997) 255-259 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702111"}> arXiv:hep-th/9702111
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(97)00365-1"} doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(97)00365-1
          %p A variant adapted to a 3+3-dimensional split in
          %ul
            %li
