          %h3#ReferencesHopfWessZuminoTerm Hopf-Wess-Zumino term
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+WZW+model"} higher WZW term
            of the M5-brane (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf-Wess-Zumino+term"}> Hopf-Wess-Zumino term
            ) was first proposed in
          %ul
            %li#Aharony94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Aharony"}> Ofer Aharony
              , p. 11 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em String theory dualities from M theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9604103"} arXiv:hep-th/9604103
          %p and had been settled by the time of
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#BLNPST97"}> BLNPST 97 (1)
              \.
          %p
            The resemblence of the first summand of the term to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+integral+formula"} Whitehead integral formula
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant"} Hopf invariant
            was noticed in
          %ul
            %li#Intriligator00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Intriligator"}> Kenneth Intriligator
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Anomaly Matching and a Hopf-Wess-Zumino Term in 6d, N=(2,0) Field Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0001205"} arXiv:hep-th/0001205
          %p which hence introduced the terminology “Hopf-Wess-Zumino term”. Followup to this terminology includes
          %ul
            %li#KalkkinenStelle02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jussi+Kalkkinen"}> Jussi Kalkkinen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Large Gauge Transformations in M-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0212081"} arXiv:hep-th/0212081
            %li
              %p
                Shan Hu, Dimitri Nanopoulos,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hopf-Wess-Zumino term in the effective action of the 6d, (2, 0) field theory revisted
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.0861"} arXiv:1110.0861
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Arvanitakis"}> Alex Arvanitakis
                , Section 4.1 of
                %em
                  Brane Wess-Zumino terms from AKSZ and exceptional generalised geometry as an
                  = succeed "-algebroid" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.07303"}> arXiv:1804.07303
                )
          %p More on the relation to the Hopf invariant in
          %ul
            %li#Sati13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Framed M-branes, corners, and topological invariants
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1060"} arXiv:1310.1060
          %p Discussion of the full 6d WZ term is in
          %ul
            %li#FSS19WZ
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Cohomotopy+implies+M5+WZ+term+level+quantization"} Twisted Cohomotopy implies M5 WZ term level quantization
          %h3#ReferencesAnomalyCancellation Anomaly cancellation
          %p The original computation of the total M5-brane anomaly due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Witten96"} Witten 96
          %p
            left a remnant term of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
